      "Language": "jpn",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Recent advancement in magnetic resonance spectroscopy (MRS) has elucidated the pathophysiology of mental illness, including schizophrenia. MRS is a neuroimaging technique that non-invasively measures chemicals, using nuclear magnetic resonance. This narrative review explains proton MRS (<sup>1<\/sup>H-MRS) and introduces pivotal studies to examine a glutamate hypothesis for schizophrenia, employing <sup>1<\/sup>H-MRS."},
